   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to directing the division of\nveterans' services to provide information to veterans who experience\npost-traumatic stress disorder and traumatic brain injury",
    "basePrintNo": "S4971",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4971-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 45,
       "fullName": "Dan Stec",
       "imgName": "674_dan_stec.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1490,
       "sessionMemberId": 1845,
       "sessionYear": 2021,
       "shortName": "STEC"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §353, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4971\n\nSPONSOR: KENNEDY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to directing the division\nof veterans' services to provide information to veterans who experience\npost-traumatic stress disorder and traumatic brain injury\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill adds post-traumatic stress disorder (PTSD) and traumatic brain\ninjury (TBI)to the list of informational portals required on the Divi-\nsion of Veterans' Services website.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends Subdivision 21 of Section 353 of the Executive Law by\nadding post-traumatic stress disorder and traumatic brain injury infor-\nmation regarding resources that are available to veterans to be included\non the Division of Veterans' Services website\n\nSection 2: Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nTraumatic brain injury (TBI) usually results from a violent blow or jolt\nto the head or body. An object that penetrates brain tissue, such as a\nbullet or shatter piece of skull can also cause traumatic brain injury.\nExplosive blasts are a common cause of TBI in active duty military\npersonnel.\n\nThis legislation requires the Division of Veterans' Services to develop\nadditional portals on their website to provide links to appropriate\ngovernment programs on information on post-traumatic stress disorder\n(PTSD) and traumatic brain injury. Providing these links will provide a\nvital service to veterans as they continue their journey of readjusting\nto civilian life.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nMinimal cost to the Division of Veterans' Services.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the sixtieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
